.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
reboot
- halt or reboot the system
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNOPSIS
.in +5
.br
.bd
reboot(howto)
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
Reboot restarts the system.  If howto has the RB_HALT bit set, the
machine is halted instead of rebooted.

Only the super-user may call reboot.

The machine is halted by dropping the cpu in kernel mode.  On real
hardware this traps to the monitor; the simulators end the run.
Only RB_HALT is implemented - there is no bootstrap to return to, so
an RB_AUTOBOOT request still halts rather than pretending to reboot.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
If the caller is not the super-user, reboot returns -1 and errno is
set to EPERM.  Otherwise it does not return.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ASSEMBLER
.in +5
.br
.bd
(reboot = 49)
.br
.bd
(howto in the instruction stream)
.br
.bd
sys; reboot
.sp 2
.in -5
